nge the season's complexion, but some coaches are coming under pressure.","published":"2026-11-15T08:17:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal111426/week-11-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Predicting the College Football Playoff: Who's most likely to make the field?","description":"Find out which teams our experts think will make this season's CFP.","published":"2026-11-15T07:48:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions111426/cfp-predictions-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lane Kiffin understands frustration as LSU's CFP hopes dashed with Texas loss","description":"Lane Kiffin said it was fair to question LSU's 6-4 record after Saturday's loss to Texas, a defeat that likely knocked the Tigers out of playoff contention.","published":"2026-11-15T15:44:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488081/kiffin-understands-frustration-lsu-playoff-hopes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5138455/jide-abasiri","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jide_Abasiri"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jide Abasiri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jide_Abasiri","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:11Z","intro":"Jide Abasiri (born March 10, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the USC Trojans.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Abasiri attended Prior Lake High School in Savage, Minnesota. As a senior in 2023, he was named the team's defensive lineman of the year and The Minnesota Star Tribune All-Metro First Team after recording 57 tackles and two sacks. He played in the Minnesota High School All-Star Game. He originally committed to play college football at the University of Minnesota before flipping his commitment to the University of Southern California (USC)."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Abasiri played in 10 games as a true freshman at USC in 2024, recording seven tackles. As a sophomore in 2025, he started nine of 13 games and had 26 tackles and 3.5 sacks. Abasiri returned to USC as a starter his junior year in 2026."}]}}